Tabs: Names -> Visibility -> Statuses -> NM Tracking -> Experimental Builder
All sections use aligned labels, common control widths and shared (?) help.
Existing per-character settings migrate once; format strings own token visibility.

Names
  General Name Appearance
    Font [dropdown]
    Bold [checkbox]
    Maximum Name Size (px) [integer, 6-48; shared by every entity type]
    Minimum Name Size (px) [integer, 6 to maximum; shared by every entity type]
    Subtarget Size (%) [slider, 50-200]
    Outline (px) [radio, 0-3]
    Health Bars [checkbox; shared by all entity types, including pets/trusts and NPCs]
    Combat Only [checkbox; defaults off, disabled while bars off]
      Requires each entity's own Engaged status (1), valid server ID and HP > 0.
      Claimed/targeted alone is insufficient. Missing status hides the bar.
    Health Bar Width (px) [integer, 12-300, default 60; shared]
    Health Bar Height (px) [integer, 3-40, default 6; shared]
  Player Names
    Player Format [text; default [icons: space=4][name]]
      (?) lists [name], [icons], [distance], options, example format and sample output.
      Example: [icons: space=4][name] ([distance: decimals=1, color=yellow]y)
      Output: [status icons] Player Name (12.4y)
    Reset Format [button, only this category]
    Colour Overrides [collapsed; each state has enable + RGB picker; defaults off]
      Normal / In Combat / Targeted / Dead
      Use Game Colours [button; disable category overrides, keep picker choices]
    Includes player-style pets/trusts. [icons] owns icon placement/visibility.
  Enemy Names
    Enemy Format [text; baseline [aggro] Lv [level]. [name]]
      (?) lists [name], [distance], [level], [aggro], [checked], [letters], options and example.
      Example: [aggro: space=4]Lv [level]. [name] [letters: type=double] ([distance: decimals=1]y)
      Output: [aggro icon] Lv 80-82. Goblin Butcher AA (12.4y)
    Reset Format [button, only this category]
    Colour Overrides [collapsed; each state has enable + RGB picker; defaults off]
      Unclaimed / Claimed: You-Party-Alliance / Claimed: Others / Targeted / Dead
      Use Game Colours [button]
    Help / Examples [collapsed letter caveats]
    Check Details [collapsed tree]
      Enabled [checkbox]
      Size (%) [slider, 50-125, while enabled]
      Abbreviate Difficulty [checkbox, while enabled]
      Display Style [dropdown, Icons & Text / Text Only, while enabled]
      Help / Examples [collapsed help, while enabled]
    No Show Level, Show Aggro, Mob Letters or Double Letters checkboxes.
    [level], [aggro], [letters] display whenever present in the format.
    [letters: type=double] continues AA, AB, etc. after Z; type=single repeats A-Z.
    Legacy [letter] remains an alias. Missing token means no letters; no automatic suffix.
  NPC Names
    NPC Format [text; default [name]]
      (?) lists [name], [distance], [icons] (when supplied), options and example.
      Example: [name: color=cyan] ([distance: decimals=1]y)
      Output: Mog House (4.2y)
    Reset Format [button, only this category]
    Colour Overrides [collapsed; each state has enable + RGB picker; defaults off]
      Normal / Targeted
      Use Game Colours [button]
  Diagnostics [collapsed]
    Enable Diagnostics [checkbox; also /name diag on/off]
    Names In View [counts, while plugin is connected]
    Custom Names, Write Log, Last Log [while diagnostics is enabled]

Name sizes, health-bar enable, dimensions and combat filter are shared across all types.
Bar dimensions include the border and stay visible but disabled while Health Bars is off.
One-time bar migration: enabled if any category enabled; dimensions use the first enabled Enemy -> Player -> NPC (Enemy if all off). Legacy per-type bars remain archived, not live.
Colours apply jointly to name, spawn letters and HP fill, overriding explicit name/letter token tints while enabled. Icons retain their colours; other explicit coloured text is unchanged.
Colour priority: Dead -> Targeted -> combat/claim -> Normal -> game/format. Dead never inherits live overrides. Opacity/fading remains client-controlled.
No separate Health Bars section, health-bar previews or Tokens & Examples dropdowns.

Token options
  All tokens: color=yellow or #RRGGBB; space=0-64 pixels after non-empty output.
  Icons: size=25-300 percent of name height; gap=0-24 pixels between icons.
  Distance: decimals=0-2, default 1.
  Letters: type=single or type=double, default single.
  Mob fields: display=raw/names/both (saved/manual formats default raw).
  Every block: when=target+checked+nm+relevant [any subset, AND]; within=1-100 yalms.
  Conditional Text blocks use generated percent-encoded [text: value=...] tokens.
  Options may be comma/semicolon/space-separated; old colour shorthand remains supported.
  Invalid options remain literal; numeric values are clamped.

Visibility
  Players: Own Name, Party Members, Alliance Members, Other Players [checkboxes]
  Pets: My Pet, Other Pets [checkboxes]
  NPCs & Monsters: NPCs, Monsters [checkboxes]
  Target: Always Show Target [checkbox]

Statuses
  Display: Enabled, Size (%), Position, Alignment, Timers, Preview
  Selected Statuses: Search, Selected Only, scrollable checkbox list with icon previews
  Help / Examples [collapsed]

NM Tracking
  Tracked Monster: Tracked NM, Target Size (%)
  Placeholder Options: Label Placeholders [when tracked monster has placeholders]

Experimental Builder [enemy names only; existing menus unchanged]
  Example [top preview; approximate badges/icons]
    Preview mob [current-zone mobdb entries, including index variants; explicit demo fallback]
    Checked, Targeted, Distant size [simulation toggles]; Distance (y)
    Uses shared General font/bold/outline/name sizes, with draft colours/check-line size. Preview /check level/difficulty are simulated.
  Builder [above block list]
    Name line [drag to reorder, insertion marker, click to select]
    Check information [same block editing, anchored below name, normal /check fade]
    Dropping outside cancels. Workspace wrapping is not live multiline rendering.
  Blocks [drag upward into matching row; click also adds]
    Name: Aggro, Level, Enemy name, Letters, Distance, Checked, Text
    Check: Difficulty, Checked level, Detection, Link information, Text
    All mobdb fields [expandable catalog]
      Name, Family, Job/SubJob IDs, MinLevel/MaxLevel, Notorious, Aggro, Link
      Sight, Sound, Blood, Magic, JA, Scent, TrueSight, Immunities, Respawn
      Drops, Steal, Despoil, Spells, Modifiers
      Individual Slashing/Piercing/H2H/Impact/Fire/Ice/Wind/Earth/Lightning/Water/Light/Dark modifiers
    Text may move between rows. Other blocks are restricted to their matching row.
  Selected block
    Tokens: Space after, inherited/named/custom colour, Remove, Move left/right
    Mob fields: Database values [raw / names / both; new blocks default names]
    Every block: Target only, Checked only, Notorious monsters only, Relevant values only, Within (y)
      Conditions combine with AND; relevant suppresses false/zero/empty and neutral modifiers.
    Text: Literal text/punctuation, colour, Remove, Move left/right
    Letters: Single A-Z / Double AA-ZZ
    Distance: Decimal places
  Check line: Enabled, Size (%), Abbreviate difficulty
  Name sizes [read from General Name Appearance; no builder overrides]
  Generated name and check formats [readable text]
  Apply to Enemy Names [explicit save; player/NPC and health-bar settings untouched]
  Reload Current [discard draft; required if live enemy settings changed]
  Session-only drafts; normal settings persistence after Apply. 24-block addition limit per row.
  Health-bar options remain in Names > Enemy Names, not in the builder.
  Empty checkFormat preserves original check renderer; regular Check Details has Restore Original Check Line.
